web888-websdr (2026.730-10) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * USB-WiFi support for the admin network page on Debian: new
    /usr/lib/web888/root-helpers/web888-wificonfig (sudoers-registered,
    verbs client|ap|ap-defaults|off) owns all config templates and applies
    them outside the service sandbox via a systemd-run transient unit;
    new patch 0023-wifi-config-debian.patch stages the admin console's
    wifi_mode/wifi_ssid/wifi_password values at init (gated on the new
    adm.wifi_configured flag set by real user edits) and invokes the
    helper. AP mode is refused with a clear error when the attached
    dongle/driver lacks AP support (the stock RTL8188EUS/rtl8xxxu does).
  * Stop shipping the vendored dumphfdl at /usr/lib/web888/dumphfdl: its
    library linkage (built from the externals/ submodule) does not match
    the Debian trixie runtime, so it cannot run. The system dumphfdl
    package is already a hard Depends; patch 0006 now launches
    /usr/bin/dumphfdl instead (renamed 0006-hfdl-system-dumphfdl.patch).
    The submodule is still compiled (ENABLE_HDFL=ON also gates the HFDL
    extension itself) but its binary is no longer installed.
  * New patch 0153-admin-status-poll-unknown-cmd-noise.patch: the 0145
    admin.js v1.902 resync added a 1 Hz status-tab poll sending
    'SET xfer_stats' and 'ADM antsw_GetCurrentAnt', which RaspSDR's
    server does not implement — it logged "ADMIN: unknown command"
    twice per second while an admin status tab was open. Both sends
    are removed; nothing ever rendered from their replies.

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:31:57 +0800

