web888-websdr (2026.730-8) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Patch 0152: never drop websocket control messages on s2c queue
    overflow. 0151 routed send_msg*() through the s2c nbuf queue whose
    stream-data watermarks (ND_HIWAT=64, ovfl latch until < 32) silently
    dropped control messages: the /admin startup burst (~200 queue
    entries: cfg frames + ~170 log_msg + 25 ext_call) overflowed it and
    the ext_call extension-config batch was lost, so the admin Extensions
    tab rendered no extensions except ant_switch (which registers its
    config independently). Nondeterministic per page load (drain-rate
    race). Adds nbuf_allocq_critical() (bypasses the ovfl latch, drops
    only past a pathological 1024-entry cap, loudly) used by
    send_msg_buf()/send_msg_mc(); audio/WF stream data keeps the original
    drop-under-backpressure behaviour.

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:10:00 +0800

web888-websdr (2026.730-7) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Patch 0151: fix probabilistic /admin websocket disconnects. The 0144
    mongoose 7.14 upgrade removed the old global mongoose_lock, and this
    port runs every kiwi task as a real pthread (support/coroutines.cpp),
    so send_msg*() from task threads raced the web server task's poll-side
    socket write on mc->send and put malformed frames on the wire
    (browser: "Received unexpected continuation frame" / "Invalid frame
    header"; server: "ADMIN connection closed" ~0.5 s after allow).
    send_msg_buf()/send_msg_mc() now queue onto the locked s2c nbuf and
    only the mongoose poll thread issues mg_ws_send().
    Analysis: docs/dev/mongoose-websocket-frame-corruption-investigation.md

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:20:00 +0800

web888-websdr (2026.730-6) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Patch 0150: re-measure SNR when the antenna selection changes.
    Restores the "Measure on antenna change" (snr_meas_ant_sw) admin
    checkbox and hooks ant_switch_setantenna()/ant_switch_toggleantenna()
    server-side to wake the SNR measurement task immediately after a
    switch (upstream triggers from the client via SET antsw_snr with a
    5 s delay; Web-888's coroutines have no delayed re-wake primitive,
    and the server-side hook also covers server-initiated switches).

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:10:00 +0800

web888-websdr (2026.730-5) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Cherry-pick 0149: port KiwiSDR's rx_snr SNR measurement framework
    (rx_snr.h/rx_snr.cpp wholesale, adapted to Web-888's scheduler and
    globals): VDSL strong-signal run filter, minute-granularity and custom
    measurement intervals, custom band definition, ham-band and AM-broadcast
    -band measurements, /snr JSON gains imin/ant fields and float band edges,
    "Measure SNR now" admin button now actually triggers an on-demand
    measurement server-side (it was a UI no-op before), SNR no longer forces
    waterfall zoom 0 for every band (per-band zoom capability, unused on
    Web-888's faster fixed waterfall). Local snd_send_msg() with
    SM_SND_ADM_ALL added so live admin pages get snr_stats spinner feedback.

